  "description": "6 x Lime (applicants ref. T1, T2, T3, T4, T5, T6) - Reduce height by 2m, raise crowns to 5m (just overgrown epicormic growth being removed). The trees are in decline, all of them have large dead branches in them. Reducing the crowns will reduce the likelihood of branch failure and let more light into the garden area. Raising the crowns will allow more light into the area, open up the space and allow for underplanting. Standing in Group G4 of Tree Preservation Order.\r\r1 x Cedar of Lebanon (applicants ref. T7) - Reduce low damaged branch by 2m. To improve likelihood of wound occlusion. Standing in T5 of Tree Preservation Order.",
